    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **30 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented a per-day owner creation cap on `POST /api/owners`: once 100 or more owners exist with today's `registrationDate`, further creates are rejected with HTTP 429.\n\nFollowing the OfficeFloor function-injection conventions in `AGENTS.md`, I modeled this on the existing city-capacity rule and added four pieces:\n\n1. **`CheckOwnerDailyLimit`** (`rest/function/owner/`) \u2014 counts stored owners whose `registrationDate` equals `LocalDate.now()` and throws the checked `DailyOwnerLimitException` at \u2265100. It runs before save, so the count excludes the owner being created (100th accepted, 101st rejected \u2014 matching how `BuildOwner` stamps `registrationDate = now`).\n\n2. **`DailyOwnerLimitException`** (`rest/escalation/`) \u2014 a checked exception so it appears in the `throws` clause.\n\n3. **`DailyOwnerLimitExceptionHandler`** \u2014 responds `429 TOO_MANY_REQUESTS`, mirroring the city handler's error-body shape.\n\n4. **Escalation YAML** wiring the exception to its handler, and a new `checkDailyLimit` step inserted into `owners.POST.yml` after `checkCityCapacity` (with `govern: [ transaction ]`, consistent with the other checks).\n\nThe pre-existing `Cp19Tests` acceptance test (create 100 \u2192 101st is 429) now passes, `Cp18Tests` (city capacity) still passes, and no other tests regressed.",
